{"id":"cmpl-geulpu-32","object":"text_completion","created":1791898635,"model":"DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B-Q8_0","choices":[{"index":0,"text":"\nOkay, so I have this problem here: \"In how many ways can a committee of 4 people be chosen from a group of 13 people?\" Hmm, let me think about how to approach this. I remember that when we're dealing with combinations, the order doesn't matter. So, if we're selecting a committee, the order in which we pick the people doesn't affect the committee itself. That makes me think that this is a combination problem, not a permutation problem.\n\nLet me recall the formula for combinations. I think it's n choose k, which is equal to n! divided by (k! times (n - k)!). So, in this case, n is 13 because there are 13 people, and k is 4 because we need to choose 4 people. So, plugging those numbers into the formula, it should be 13 choose 4, which is 13! divided by (4! times (13 - 4)!).\n\nWait, let me make sure I got that right. So, 13 choose 4 is 13! / (4! * 9!). Yeah, that seems correct because 13 - 4 is 9. So, the denominator is 4! times 9!. Now, I need to compute that. But 13! is a huge number, so maybe I can simplify it before calculating.\n\nLet me write out 13! as 13 × 12 × 11 × 10 × 9!. Oh, wait, that's helpful because the 9! in the denominator will cancel out with the 9! in the numerator. So, that simplifies things a lot. So, now, 13! / (4! * 9!) becomes (13 × 12 × 11 × 10 × 9!) / (4! × 9!). The 9! cancels out, leaving us with (13 × 12 × 11 × 10) / 4!.\n\nOkay, so now I need to compute 13 × 12 × 11 × 10 divided by 4!. Let me compute the numerator first. 13 multiplied by 12 is 156. Then, 156 multiplied by 11 is... let me see, 156 × 10 is 1560, plus 156 is 1716. Then, 1716 multiplied by 10 is 17160. So, the numerator is 17160.\n\nNow, the denominator is 4!, which is 4 × 3 × 2 × 1. Let me compute that: 4 × 3 is 12, 12 × 2 is 24, 24 × 1 is 24. So, 4! is 24.\n\nSo, now, I have 17160 divided by 24. Hmm, let me do that division. 17160 ÷ 24. Let me see, 24 × 700 is 16800. Subtracting that from 17160, we get 17160 - 16800 = 360. Now, 24 × 15 is 360. So, adding that to 700, we get 715. So, 17160 ÷ 24 is 715.\n\nTherefore, the number of ways to choose a committee of 4 people from 13 is 715. Let me just double-check my calculations to make sure I didn't make a mistake. So, 13 × 12 × 11 × 10 is indeed 17160, and 4! is 24. Dividing 17160 by 24 gives 715. Yeah, that seems right.\n\nAlternatively, I can think about this problem step by step. When choosing 4 people out of 13, the first person can be chosen in 13 ways, the second in 12, the third in 11, and the fourth in 10. So, that's 13 × 12 × 11 × 10, which is 17160. But since the order doesn't matter in a committee, I need to divide by the number of ways the 4 people can be arranged, which is 4! or 24. So, again, 17160 ÷ 24 is 715. Yep, same result.\n\nI think that's solid. So, the answer is 715 ways.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe number of ways is \\boxed{715}.\n\n\nTo determine the number of ways to choose a committee of 4 people from a group of 13 people, we use the combination formula, which is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k! \\cdot (n - k)!}\n\\]\n\nHere, \\( n = 13 \\) and \\( k = 4 \\). Plugging these values into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{13}{4} = \\frac{13!}{4! \\cdot 9!}\n\\]\n\nWe can simplify this by recognizing that \\( 13! = 13 \\times 12 \\times 11 \\times 10 \\times 9! \\). Thus, the \\( 9! \\) terms cancel out:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{13 \\times 12 \\times 11 \\times 10 \\times 9!}{4! \\times 9!} = \\frac{13 \\times 12 \\times 11 \\times 10}{4!}\n\\]\n\nCalculating the numerator:\n\n\\[\n13 \\times 12 = 156\n\\]\n\\[\n156 \\times 11 = 1716\n\\]\n\\[\n1716 \\times 10 = 17160\n\\]\n\nCalculating the denominator:\n\n\\[\n4! = 4 \\times 3 \\times 2 \\times 1 = 24\n\\]\n\nDividing the numerator by the denominator:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{17160}{24} = 715\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of ways to choose a committee of 4 people from a group of 13 is \\(\\boxed{715}\\).","logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":40,"completion_tokens":1441,"total_tokens":1481},"geulpu":{"seed":5986621760054604904,"tokens":[151648,198,32313,11,773,358,614,419,3491,1588,25,330,641,1246,1657,5510,646,264,12801,315,220,19,1251,387,11882,504,264,1874,315,220,16,18,1251,7521,88190,11,1077,752,1744,911,1246,311,5486,419,13,358,6099,429,979,582,2299,14550,448,27459,11,279,1973,3171,944,4925,13,2055,11,421,582,2299,26301,264,12801,11,279,1973,304,892,582,3735,279,1251,3171,944,7802,279,12801,5086,13,2938,3643,752,1744,429,419,374,264,10601,3491,11,537,264,58441,3491,382,10061,752,19091,279,14806,369,27459,13,358,1744,432,594,308,5157,595,11,892,374,6144,311,308,0,17779,553,320,74,0,3039,320,77,481,595,41295,568,2055,11,304,419,1142,11,308,374,220,16,18,1576,1052,525,220,16,18,1251,11,323,595,374,220,19,1576,582,1184,311,5157,220,19,1251,13,2055,11,625,35268,1846,5109,1119,279,14806,11,432,1265,387,220,16,18,5157,220,19,11,892,374,220,16,18,0,17779,553,320,19,0,3039,320,16,18,481,220,19,41295,3593,14190,11,1077,752,1281,2704,358,2684,429,1290,13,2055,11,220,16,18,5157,220,19,374,220,16,18,0,608,320,19,0,353,220,24,42392,21607,11,429,4977,4396,1576,220,16,18,481,220,19,374,220,24,13,2055,11,279,46912,374,220,19,0,3039,220,24,15365,4695,11,358,1184,311,12564,429,13,1988,220,16,18,0,374,264,6765,1372,11,773,7196,358,646,39721,432,1573,37614,382,10061,752,3270,700,220,16,18,0,438,220,16,18,24768,220,16,17,24768,220,16,16,24768,220,16,15,24768,220,24,15365,8670,11,3783,11,429,594,10950,1576,279,220,24,0,304,279,46912,686,9121,700,448,279,220,24,0,304,279,63533,13,2055,11,429,15491,9606,2513,264,2696,13,2055,11,1431,11,220,16,18,0,608,320,19,0,353,220,24,16315,9044,320,16,18,24768,220,16,17,24768,220,16,16,24768,220,16,15,24768,220,24,16315,608,320,19,0,24768,220,24,42392,576,220,24,0,62309,2010,700,11,9380,601,448,320,16,18,24768,220,16,17,24768,220,16,16,24768,220,16,15,8,608,220,19,98527,32313,11,773,1431,358,1